---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const hosts = [
  {
    name: 'GitHub Pages',
    target: 'username.github.io',
    note: 'Free forever, works with a repo',
    href: '/guide/github-pages',
  },
  {
    name: 'Cloudflare Pages',
    target: 'project.pages.dev',
    note: 'Free, fast, custom domains',
    href: '/guide/cloudflare-pages',
  },
  {
    name: 'Vercel',
    target: 'project.vercel.app',
    note: 'Great for Next.js portfolios',
    href: '/guide/vercel',
  },
  {
    name: 'Netlify',
    target: 'site.netlify.app',
    note: 'Free tier, drag-and-drop deploy',
    href: '/guide/netlify',
  },
];
---

<Base>
<section class="hero">
  <h1>Give your portfolio a name worth sharing.</h1>
  <p class="lead narrow">
    You already built the site. We give it a clean
    <strong>yourname.filipino-talent.com</strong> address and point it at the host
    you already use. No DNS knowledge needed — we handle that part.
  </p>
  <p class="hero-demo" aria-label="Example of a finished address">
    <span>juan-dela-cruz</span><span class="host">.filipino-talent.com</span>
  </p>
  <p class="row mt-6" style="gap:10px">
    <a class="btn" href="/submit">Get your subdomain</a>
    <a class="btn secondary" href="/guide">How it works</a>
  </p>
  <ul class="trust-row">
    <li>Takes about 2 minutes</li>
    <li>Free, no catch</li>
    <li>Nothing is published until you confirm it is yours</li>
    <li>Remove it anytime</li>
  </ul>
  <p id="proof" class="muted" hidden style="margin-top:18px;font-size:.95rem"></p>
</section>

<hr />

<section>
  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      <strong>Pick a name and submit.</strong> A subdomain is just the part before
      the dot — like <code>juan-dela-cruz</code>. Tell us the name you want, your
      portfolio URL, and where it is hosted.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>It goes live.</strong> Your address is published automatically,
      usually within 15 minutes. Email <code>verify@filipino-talent.com</code>
      from the address on your portfolio so we can confirm it is yours.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Connect it at your host.</strong> Tell GitHub Pages, Cloudflare
      Pages, Vercel, or Netlify to answer for the subdomain. Our
      <a href="/guide/connect">one-page guide</a> walks you through it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Keep it, or pass it on.</strong> It is yours for as long as you
      need it. Once you can afford your own domain, release it for the next
      person.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p class="muted mt-5">
    No portfolio online yet? Follow our free
    <a href="/guide/github-pages">GitHub Pages setup</a> first, then come back.
  </p>
</section>

<hr />

<section>
  <h2>Works with the host you already use</h2>
  <ul class="host-list">
    {hosts.map((h) => (
      <li>
        <a class="host-list-item" href={h.href}>
          <span class="host-list-name">{h.name}</span>
          <span class="host-list-target mono">{h.target}</span>
          <span class="host-list-note muted">{h.note}</span>
          <span class="host-list-go">Set it up →</span>
        </a>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p class="muted mt-5">
    Using Wix, Canva, or WordPress.com? They need a paid plan and their own DNS,
    so they are not supported here. See
    <a href="/guide/canva">free alternatives</a>.
  </p>
</section>

<div class="band pass-on">
  <div>
    <h2>This is a gift. Pass it on.</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:0">
      filipino-talent.com is a free service for Filipino remote workers. Once you
      can afford a domain of your own, email
      <a href="mailto:remove@filipino-talent.com">remove@filipino-talent.com</a>
      to release your name for the next person climbing the same path.
    </p>
  </div>
  <p style="margin:0">
    <a class="btn secondary" href="/directory">See who already has one</a>
  </p>
</div>

<aside class="band" style="text-align:left">
  <h2 style="font-size:1.15rem">Who this is for</h2>
  <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:0">
    This service is for Filipino remote workers. Requests from outside that
    community may be declined. filipino-talent.com is an independent community
    project — not a job board, and not affiliated with any employer, agency, or
    organization. A subdomain implies no endorsement or employment.
  </p>
</aside>

<section class="card center" style="margin-top:32px">
  <h2 class="mt-0">Ready to look professional?</h2>
  <p class="muted">It takes about two minutes. No cost, no catch.</p>
  <p style="margin-top:16px">
    <a class="btn" href="/submit">Get your subdomain</a>
  </p>
</section>

<script>
  const API = (import.meta.env.PUBLIC_API_BASE ?? 'https://api.filipino-talent.com').replace(/\/$/, '');
  fetch(`${API}/domains`)
    .then((r) => (r.ok ? r.json() : null))
    .then((data) => {
      const n = Array.isArray(data?.domains) ? data.domains.length : 0;
      const el = document.getElementById('proof');
      if (!el || n <= 0) return;
      el.textContent =
        n === 1
          ? '1 creator has already claimed a subdomain.'
          : `${n} creators have already claimed a subdomain.`;
      el.hidden = false;
    })
    .catch(() => {});
</script>
</Base>
